    "id": "rtc-ds3231-module",
    "name": "DS3231 high-precision RTC module (ZS-042)",
    "category": "sensor",
    "description": "Temperature-compensated real-time clock: ±2 ppm between 0-40 °C (about ±1 minute per year), seconds/minutes/hours/day/date/month/year with leap-year correction, on-chip aging trim and an integrated temperature sensor readable over I2C. The ZS-042 breakout adds a CR2032 backup holder so time survives power loss, plus SQW and 32K output pins. Careful on a shared bus: the DS3231 answers at 0x68 — the SAME address as an MPU6050. Move the IMU to 0x69 (AD0 high) or use one or the other.",
